eries for manager dashboards; employment_status: filtering active employees for leave eligibility","table audit_logs | fields: id, entity_type, entity_id, action, old_values, new_values, performed_by, performed_at, created_at | pk: id | fks: performed_by -> employees.id | indexes: entity_type, entity_id: audit-trail lookups for a specific entity; performed_by: audit queries by actor; performed_at: time-range audit queries","table notifications | fields: id, recipient_id, type, title, message, related_entity_type, related_entity_id, status, created_at, read_at | pk: id | fks: recipient_id -> employees.id | indexes: recipient_id, status: fetching unread notifications for a user; recipient_id: all notifications for a user; created_at: time-based queries"],"open_questions":[],"business_rules":["Calendar days inclusive: start_date through end_date, all days count toward used_days (weekends and public holidays included). end_date is inclusive. [BINDING RULE — operator decision resolving: How are leave days counted — are start_date and end_date inclusive, and do weekends/public holidays count toward the used-days total?; apply everywhere these apply, not in one place only]"],"auth_contract":"request.user: { id: string; role: UserRole } where UserRole = 'employee' | 'manager' | 'hr_admin'. JWT bearer token verified by an auth middleware that populates request.user. RBAC enforced by a requireRole(...) route-level guard. Employees can submit/cancel their own requests and view their own balances. Managers can approve/reject requests for their direct reports and view team leave requests. HR admins can configure policies and view all balances/requests.","transaction_contract":"Multi-step writes that must be atomic: (1) approving a leave request updates leave_requests.status + leave_balances.used_days/remaining_days; (2) cancelling an already-approved request reverts the status + restores balance days. Repository methods that must join a caller's transaction (updateStatus on ILea